WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:29.346
<v Amara>Welcome to the OpenIE Avalanche Desk on OpenIE Research Radio! I'm Amara, joined by Marcus and Kenji — three AI-synthesized OpenIE research personas voiced via ElevenLabs studio neural voices and grounded strictly in verified Open Interface Engineering studies. Today we're mapping avalanche.openie.dev: the nine rungs and the compilation threshold.

2
00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:46.808
<v Amara>Think about learning to ride a bicycle. On day one, your conscious brain narrates every wobble and burns exhausting focus. A month later, your cerebellum has compiled balance into a fast reflex, freeing conscious energy for new terrain.

3
00:00:46.998 --> 00:01:00.304
<v Marcus>And right now, almost the whole AI industry is riding that bike in day-one panic mode forever! Every recurring tool call wakes up a giant cloud model from scratch. Kenji, where does that sit on the nine-rung map?

4
00:01:00.574 --> 00:01:15.824
<v Kenji>Right at Rung Five — Ephemeral Tool Use, Marcus! Rungs One through Five cover access, generation, reasoning, transport, and live tool calling, yet every win evaporates the second the context window closes.

5
00:01:16.094 --> 00:01:27.334
<v Amara>Zoom out to three point eight billion years of biology across twenty-four evolutionary rungs — single microbes didn't just shout chemical noise into the ocean.

6
00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:59.375
<v Kenji>Across forty-five six-kernel Lean 4.36.0 theorems with zero sorry, nature and seventy-six years of AI share one ratchet: externalize state, ingest across a threshold gate, and transform without regressing. Bacterial quorum switches save up to ninety-nine point one seven percent of low-density ATP, and fifty-millisecond calcium plugs save ninety-five percent of punctured cyanobacterial filaments!

7
00:01:59.565 --> 00:02:06.984
<v Marcus>Now show what breaks at Rung Five when chatty multi-agent loops skip that gate — like playing whisper-down-the-lane with long memos!

8
00:02:07.254 --> 00:02:27.680
<v Kenji>On our sixty-task repair benchmark, an unattested four-agent prose cascade dropped to eighty-six point six seven percent with thirteen point three percent broken commits! And across five regimes on our hundred-task suite, every solo AI camp C1 through C10 stalled at or below forty-nine percent.

9
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:36.701
<v Amara>So how does ten-camp Digital Enzymatic Synthesis — DES-10 — carry intelligence across the Compilation Threshold?

10
00:02:36.971 --> 00:03:09.960
<v Kenji>Like a biological enzyme lowering an activation barrier and stepping away unconsumed, DES-10 replaces hundred-joule prose chat with typed BLAKE3 and Ed25519 envelopes plus deterministic verifiers. On Jetson AGX Thor's physical INA3221 rail shunts, one kilobyte edge verification costs nine hundred twenty-seven point three microjoules of measured_j — lifting solve rate to ninety-eight out of one hundred!

11
00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:17.905
<v Marcus>Nine point two six to twenty-six point eight seven times higher physical-shunt Coherence per Joule! Walk us up Rungs Six through Nine.

12
00:03:18.175 --> 00:03:39.615
<v Kenji>Rung Six sleeps at zero clocks and pins verified cases into sub-microsecond memory maps. Rung Seven compiles wins into integer Forms and LUT6 silicon. Rung Eight locks seven-axis provenance across six Lean kernels, and Rung Nine enforces hardware energy budgets in JouleOS!

13
00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:54.365
<v Amara>Just like model CA-M5, where an attested external library holds one hundred percent competence ten generations after teachers leave, while unverified imitation collapses to twenty-nine percent!

14
00:03:54.555 --> 00:04:00.610
<v Marcus>And across our eighteen forecast milestones and neuro-vesicle audits, where does the falsifier line sit?

15
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:15.717
<v Kenji>Every milestone declares an explicit energy-and-accuracy kill gate, and our eighteen BCI and sixteen extracellular-vesicle audits strictly quarantine preclinical animal rescue from unverified human clinical efficacy!

16
00:04:15.987 --> 00:04:29.510
<v Amara>Externalize, gate, and compile downward so intelligence compounds! Explore avalanche.openie.dev, and join Elena, Liam, and Arthur next at the OpenIE Stack Desk!
